ogic, or a case `plan.md` named), smaller gaps are `medium`. The verdict is `changes` exactly when a finding blocks. `line` is the head-side line: a `+` line goes inline, anything else in the body. It writes only `review-eng-review.md` with `role: eng-review`, `attempt: 1`, `status` `done` or `needs-human`, `findings` with a double-quoted `file` and a `message: |` block, never `next` or `worker`, and a body with a `## Checks` section. It answers `needs-human` only when there is nothing to review or the issue and the plan contradict each other. The starter override is Sonnet 5.5 with the default 30m timeout and no `when:`, so every PR from the starter worker gets it. It ships no Dockerfile, so it runs as a host subprocess with the #84 warning until #55.\n../../docs/proposal.md:337:| eng-review | always | lint and coverage of added lines (the repo's own commands, run by the agent) | correctness, missing tests, drift from `plan.md` |\n../../docs/proposal.md:411:  workers/engineer:         { tests: make test, timeout: 60m, reviewers: [security-review, eng-review] }\n../../docs/proposal.md:420:**`ard init` proposes the starter `.ard/` as a PR (decided, #27).** It builds `config.yaml` and the starter roles in memory (today `scanners/cve`, `scanners/error-codes`, `triage/lead`, `triage/engineer`, `workers/engineer` and `reviewers/eng-review`; `intake: {mode: label}`, the protected-path defaults above, and the cve, error-codes, lead, engineer, worker and eng-review overrides), compares them with `main`, commits them on a new branch `ard-init` cut from `main` through the effect layer and a narrow committer lane, pushes it and opens a PR. It writes nothing to the local working tree or to `main`, and `scan` is committed `100755`. Files that already exist on `main` with different contents are a conflict naming the paths; `--force` proposes overwriting them, and init never deletes anything. It refuses while `ard-init` exists on the remote, whatever its PR's state, so it never force-pushes over or stacks commits on a human's edits: merge or close the PR, delete the branch and rerun. If `main` already has every starter file it prints `nothing to propose`. It syncs the label catalogue first (like `ard labels sync`), so a failure leaves nothing pushed. With `--dry-run` the commit, push and PR are logged to the ledger instead of acting. A missing repo, credentials or `main` branch exits 1 with nothing written, and `ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN` auth is refused outside `--dry-run`. The PR body carries the one step the App cannot do: copy `.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml` and set the repository variable `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` (optionally `ARD_BOT_CHECK_SINCE`). It also says to merge with **Squash and merge** or **Create a merge commit**, never a fast-forward from the command line, which would put the bot's commit on main's first-parent history. **Rebase and merge** is also safe: the scratch-repo run (#85) showed GitHub records the merging human as committer of a rebase-merged commit (the bot stays the author), and the bot-commit check keys on committer, so it does not flag it. The body still names only the two merges above.\n../../docs/proposal.md:481:    P0[\"Phase 0: Skeleton<br/>controller and config<br/>label bootstrap<br/>committer, local executor<br/>cve and stale scanners<br/>dry-run mode\"] -->|\"Gate 1: 1 week dry-run, 0 duplicate issues\"| P1[\"Phase 1: First loop<br/>lead + engineer triage<br/>engineer worker<br/>eng-review<br/>Reaper<br/>human approval gate\"]\nagent.go\nagent_test.go\nclaude\nerrors.go","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"585f4409-edde-4024-8727-99d6af20933b","uuid":"8285ad1c-3c40-4f7b-8eb0-ab0ea0d56420","timestamp":"2026-11-23T16:43:08.565Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"80:  GitHub or moves HEAD or a ref, and do not route around this with scripts\n90:2. For every changed file, read enough of the surrounding code to judge\n   13813 reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\neng_review_test.go:21:func reviewJob() closeou